      {
        "review_id": 462477188,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r462477188-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Impermanence",
        "text": "Pashupatinath Temple and burning ghats are beautiful, spiritual, and extremely moving, all at the same time.  It is important, in my opinion, to remember that there are families of people who are cremating their dearest relatives.  The amount of grief, some days, is palpable.  As you walk around, you will observe the Saddhus who sit and witness the cremations and are always willing to be photographed.  One Saddhu with whom I spoke, told me he had not cut his hair in 45 years!!!  There is a row of Lingams/Yonis that is truly something to behold.  It is a place of fertility on the banks of the Bagmati River, which is sacred to Hindus and Buddhists.  Pashupatinath is a rare, unique, and beautiful experience.",
        "review_tip": null,
