      {
        "review_id": 461689519,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r461689519-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Good to visit and appreciate",
        "text": "I hired a guide to wander the complex and it was useful to have this local knowledge available plus explain the Hindu faith in greater detail.\nNon-Hindus can not enter the main temple however, that is the only restriction.\nSeeing the Bagmati river site where the cremations take place is interesting. As a westerner I'm used to the more closed approach to death and seeing a more open, public ceremony is interesting. I didn't find the experience macabre or feel a voyeur. \nWho is to say one approach is better than another? We come from the earth and we return there... in this case as ash.\nI would recommend anyone to visit.",
